{# The certified RESULT block (docs/RESULTS.md, Rendering § Race cards, #286;
   § The race-detail page, #370), rendered from one `context.RaceResultsView`
   — built by `race_results_view(race, ...)` — the same way the segmented
   meter is rendered from one `MeterView` (`_meter.html.j2`).

   Both pages that render it (`guide.html.j2`'s race card, below its own rule;
   `race.html.j2`'s race page, under the race header and above the lens bar)
   import this macro rather than carrying their own copy. They carried
   identical copies for exactly as long as it took to write the second one:
   the block is one component stating one fact, its paint is single-sourced
   in `guide-race.css`, and a one-sided edit here would ship a silent
   card-versus-page divergence that no check in this repository can see —
   `race-markup-parity.test.mjs` diffs the server against lit, and no client
   module renders `.race-results` at all.

   `view.outcomes` is every choice on the ballot in finish order, not only the
   endorsed ones. On a race card that is simply the whole tally; on a race
   page it is the entire reason the block exists, since a winner nobody
   endorsed has no candidate section to carry a result.

   `section_candidate_ids` names the choices that have a section on this page,
   whose tally row then links down to it. Empty by default, which is the race
   card: the guide has no candidate sections to reach, and the card's whole
   recommendation area is already one link to the race's page, so a link here
   would nest inside it. The same emptiness is why the parameter names the
   choices rather than the page — a choice nobody endorsed has no section on
   either surface, and its name stays plain rather than pointing at an anchor
   that is not there.

   Each page keeps its own frame around this markup — the card's rule, which
   is the block's own default (guide-race.css), and the page's tone band,
   which switches that default off (`.race-detail-certified-result`,
   race.css) — and its own
   `{% raw %}{% if %}{% endraw %}` gate, because the frame is the page's and the gate is where
   each page decides it has a result to state.

   `external_link_attributes` is read from the environment globals rather than
   passed in, the convention `_shell.html.j2` states and its own macros
   follow: passing it per call would silently cover only the callers that
   remembered to.

   The indentation below is the guide card's own, so that extracting this
   macro left the guide's rendered bytes alone. Nothing pins that — no
   results file is committed, so the guide's parity fixture carries no
   `.race-results` at all and the release screenshots cannot see whitespace;
   it is a courtesy to the diff, not a checked invariant. #}
{% macro result_block(view, section_candidate_ids=()) -%}
<div class="race-results">
              <div class="race-results-head">
                <span class="race-results-eyebrow">Result</span>
                <span class="race-results-status">Certified · {{ view.certified_on_label }}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="race-results-tally">
                {% for outcome in view.outcomes %}
                {% set linked = outcome.candidate_id in section_candidate_ids %}
                <div class="race-results-row{{ '' if outcome.advanced else ' race-results-row-trailing' }}">
                  <span class="race-results-name">{% if linked %}<a href="#candidate-{{ outcome.candidate_id }}">{{ outcome.candidate_label }}</a>{% else %}{{ outcome.candidate_label }}{% endif %}{% if outcome.chip_label %} <span class="race-detail-result-chip">{{ outcome.chip_label }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
                  <span class="race-results-share">{{ outcome.percentage_label }}</span>
                  <span class="race-results-bar"><i style="width:{{ outcome.percentage_label }}"></i></span>
                </div>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
              <p class="race-results-provenance">{{ view.count_label }} · {{ view.authority }}{% if view.capture_url %} · <a href="{{ view.capture_url }}"{{ external_link_attributes }}>evidence</a>{% endif %}</p>
            </div>
{%- endmacro %}
